00:00:05.269 --> 00:00:07.190 align:start position:0%
eu ministers meet on tuesday at the  education youth culture and sport  council the meeting will start with a  cultural session where the council is  due to adopt conclusions on the european  audio visual policy in the digital era  their aim is to facilitate the supply of  high quality audio visual content meet  audience demands anywhere in the eu and  ensure equal conditions for all audio  visual media service providers  the adoption of the conclusions comes at  a strategic moment since the creation of  a digital single market is among the top  priorities of the new commission  the council will also establish a work  plan for culture setting out the  priorities for european corporation in  cultural policy making for the next four  years  furthermore conclusions will be adopted  on participatory governance of cultural  heritage  the idea that member states promote a  more active involvement of members of  society and the private sector in this  project  a debate will also take place on the  contribution of cultural and creative  sectors towards the europe 2020  objectives  ministers will discuss how those sectors  can help create a smart sustainable and  inclusive growth and stimulate social  and economic innovation  in the afternoon eu ministers for sport  will address the issue of innovation in  the sector and its positive effects on  the economy as a whole  you
 

